\title{Precompiles}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Hand-written circuits for hot operations — hashes, elliptic-curve arithmetic, big-integer work — invoked from the VM instead of being proved instruction by instruction. Large speedups, and a large increase in the amount of hand-written constrained code that has to be correct.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The mechanism: how a precompile attaches to the trace and how its inputs and outputs are tied to VM state.}
        \li{The speedups claimed, and on which workloads they decide the benchmark.}
        \li{The soundness surface: an under-constrained precompile is a complete break, with no compiler to catch it.}
        \li{Extensibility as a design goal, and what a user-supplied precompile has to prove.}
        \li{Why this is the most valuable place in the stack to point [Clean](dhsorens-002Y) at.}
    }
}
